      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "## Vendor / adapter observability (Nokia-first)\n\n### What this dashboard is for\n\n- **Bounded observability** for the **current Nokia-first gNMI collector** path and the **`app-api` collector boundary**—the same metric families exercised by `verify-core-runtime.sh` for collector and backend contracts.\n- **Not** a multi-vendor adapter matrix, **not** a claim of Juniper or broad parity, and **not** a substitute for the capability matrix in `app-web`.\n\n### Current reality (Phase 2)\n\n- **Nokia-first** observed-state collection through **`gnmi-collector`**; roadmap-only Juniper targets remain **out of scope** for honest metric-backed panels here.\n- Charts below use **real PromQL only** against metrics that already exist; where no honest series exists, this dashboard does **not** invent queries.\n\n### What Grafana is not\n\n- **Not** workflow, validation, or change-control semantics.\n- **Not** the surface that defines vendor support posture—that remains **`app-api`** contracts and **`app-web`**.\n\n### Related documentation\n\n- **`platform/docs/dashboards.md`** — vendor family scope and product vs observability split.\n- **`platform/docs/services.md`** — `gnmi-collector` role and adapter boundaries.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.0.0",
      "title": "Dashboard Scope",
      "type": "text"
    },
